# कल read as TOMORROW.  कल names both yesterday and tomorrow (CLDR 47,
# locale hi, relative-type--1 and relative-type-1), and only the verb's tense
# separates them (native answer, chronologia#1484, comment 7209012484).  The
# hook chronologia.extract.numfold_indic rewrites कल to this token when a verb
# from marker_tense_future.voc follows it.  It is not a word a speaker writes.
कल_भविष्य
